# Docker build context exclusions for the backend image.
#
# The build context is ./backend (see docker-compose.yml). Before this file
# existed, `COPY . .` shipped the whole 217MB directory into the image --
# including a 177MB scraper cache, the log directory and the test suite, none
# of which the running service reads.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DO NOT ADD `backend/` OR ANY GLOB THAT MATCHES backend/backend/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The nested `backend/backend/` path looks like a mistake and is not. It holds
# the ONLY copy of the live PCA model:
#
#     backend/backend/models/pca/pca_model_v1.pkl
#     backend/backend/models/pca/pca_metadata_v1.json
#
# app/utils/pca_loader.py::_default_pca_dir() resolves <backend>/backend/models/pca
# FIRST and only then falls back to <backend>/models/pca. Excluding it produces
# an image with no PCA model, which degrades matching rather than failing
# cleanly. It is deliberately NOT excluded here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Scraper cache -- 177MB of scraped postings. Tracked in git on purpose (it is
# the only copy of that data), but the service never reads it at runtime, so it
# has no business in the image.
.cache/

# Logs are runtime output, not build input.
logs/
*.log

# Tests and test scaffolding are not run inside the shipped image.
tests/
pytest.ini
.pytest_cache/

# Python bytecode / packaging noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Local env / secrets -- must never enter an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*credential*
*credentials*

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# VCS
.git/
.gitignore
